[41.937698, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> +\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[41.93772, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[41.938038, "o", "+    The cursor is an opaque base64url string containing the ``created_at`` timestamp and the ``id``\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[41.938067, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[41.938359, "o", "+    of the row, separated by a ``|``. Both parts are needed to create a total ordering that matches\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[41.938378, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[41.938392, "o", "> "]
[41.938627, "o", "+    the ``ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC`` clause used in the SQL queries.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[41.938644, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[41.938658, "o", "> "]
[41.93868, "o", "+    \"\"\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[41.938702, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[41.938726, "o", "> "]
[41.938856, "o", "+    raw = f\"{row['created_at']}|{row['id']}\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[41.938881, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[41.939137, "o", "+    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(raw.encode(\"ascii\")).decode(\"ascii\").rstrip(\"=\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
